# Release signing config for Self Budget.
#
# 1. Generate your own keystore (do this once, on your own machine - never ask anyone else to
#    generate or hold this for you):
#
#      keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore selfbudget-release.jks -alias selfbudget \
#        -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000
#
#    keytool will prompt you for a store password, a key password, and your distinguished-name
#    details (name/org/etc). Pick strong, unique passwords and save them in a password manager
#    immediately - this file/keystore is the ONLY thing that lets you ship an update to an app
#    already published on Google Play. If you lose it after your first Play Store upload, you
#    cannot recover it and cannot update that app listing ever again (short of Google's upload-key
#    reset process, which only applies if you already enrolled in Play App Signing).
#
# 2. Copy this file to `keystore.properties` (same directory, already git-ignored) and fill in
#    the real values below - do NOT put real passwords in this .example file.
#
# 3. Move the .jks file itself somewhere outside the repo (or keep it here - it's git-ignored -
#    but back it up separately regardless; losing the repo should not mean losing the keystore).

storeFile=../selfbudget-release.jks
storePassword=CHANGE_ME
keyAlias=selfbudget
keyPassword=CHANGE_ME
